{
  "title": "04 — Authentication, protection and delivery",
  "description": "Source-linked interview study tour. Read the highlighted code, then explain it in your own words.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "file": "apps/web/src/lib/auth.ts",
      "line": 113,
      "description": "The browser attaches an access token and can attempt one refresh on 401. Trace storage and retry decisions; do not describe access tokens as encrypted or always HttpOnly."
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/api/src/modules/auth/auth.service.ts",
      "line": 83,
      "description": "Inspect Argon2id password hashing and verification-code creation. Hashing passwords differs from encrypting a recoverable secret."
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/api/src/modules/auth/auth.service.ts",
      "line": 314,
      "description": "Follow refresh token hashing, session lookup and rotation. Explain why a signed JWT does not make the whole system stateless."
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/api/src/express/middleware/auth.ts",
      "line": 12,
      "description": "Authentication verifies tokens and reloads account status; role checks and resource ownership answer separate authorization questions. Frontend buttons are not security enforcement."
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/api/src/common/cache/cache.service.ts",
      "line": 17,
      "description": "Distinguish optional public caching from shared AI protection. Read failure behaviour rather than claiming every Redis failure is safe to ignore."
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/api/src/express/middleware/ai-guard.ts",
      "line": 16,
      "description": "Inspect the guard before AI generation: account limits, global limits, concurrent work and failure behaviour protect a bounded external resource."
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/api/src/config/sentry.ts",
      "line": 13,
      "description": "Monitoring is optional and configuration-dependent. Follow the scrubbers before discussing logs or sending request data to an external tracker."
    },
    {
      "file": ".github/workflows/ci.yml",
      "line": 9,
      "description": "One workflow job contains several steps. A failed test step can fail the job and skip later checks. CI verifies a revision; deployment and runtime health are separate."
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/worker/src/index.ts",
      "line": 34,
      "description": "Read what is actually registered: the worker is scaffolding. Describe future queue-based work as an alternative, not an already operating feature."
    }
  ]
}
